claim.claim-text:
a. obtaining a measurement of the work exerted for the inspiratory breath cycle of a selected breath of a patient;
b. setting a desired value for the level of work during contraction of the diaphragm, transmitting a stimulation signal to an electrode positioned percutaneously within tissue of the patient such that the electrode recruits a phrenic nerve of the patient and contracts the diaphragm;
c. after transmitting the stimulation signal, determining the actual work generated by the diaphragm;
d. as a function of wye flow, pressure and patient resistance and compliance, either
i) maintaining the stimulation signal value for later selected breaths if the actual value of the level of the diaphragm work is within a selected range of the desired value, or
ii) modifying the stimulation signal if the actual value of diaphragm work is outside the selected range of the desired value of diaphragm work; and

an electrode pair (38) configured to be positioned proximate to at least one phrenic nerve in the neck of said patient;
a stimulator/controller (12) configured to deliver electrical stimulation to said electrode pair at a pulse repetition rate, with a current and a waveform sufficient to at least partially activate the patient's diaphragm;
an instrumented wye (14) configured to be coupled to said patient and configured to be coupled to said mechanical ventilator, the instrumented wye configured to provide a wye flow measurement and a wye pressure measurement to said stimulator/controller (12);
wherein said stimulator/controller is configured to
select one of several breaths defining a single selected breath,
begin stimulation at the beginning of an inspiratory event in response to an inspiratory trigger event, said event corresponding to a preset specific flow at said instrumented wye, and
end stimulation at the end of an inspiratory event triggered by an end inspiratory trigger event, said event corresponding to a specific flow at said instrumented wye,
